xies, no credit card required to claim them."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What APIs and features are available on every plan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Every plan, including PAYG, gets the full ScrapeBadger product with no feature tiers: all active scrapers (new ones launch on every plan immediately), anti-bot bypass for all 6 systems, residential proxies in 150+ countries, JS rendering with stealth browser, and the MCP Server for AI agents. The only differences between plans are credit volume, per-credit rate, and rate limits."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between PAYG and a subscription?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Pay As You Go is a prepaid wallet: you top up from $10 at $0.15 per 1,000 credits and use them at your own pace (they do not expire). Subscriptions are monthly or annual plans (Starter, Growth, Pro, Scale, Volume, Max) that include a fixed monthly credit allowance at a heavily discounted rate, plus higher request-per-minute limits."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I switch plans or cancel?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes: upgrade, downgrade, or cancel at any time from your billing dashboard. Upgrades take effect immediately and restart your billing cycle that day — you pay the full new plan price, and get the full new credit allowance on top of whatever credits you have left, so the unused part of your current plan carries over as credits. Downgrades and cancellations take effect at the end of the current billing period. There are no lock-in contracts and no cancellation fees."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How are credits calculated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Each API endpoint has a fixed credit cost per successful request, and a few (such as Twitter/X) also charge per item returned. Full searches and detail lookups cost the most; autocomplete and small lookups cost less, and reference calls such as market and category lists are free. A Web Scraping API request is priced by its engine and proxy tier. Failed requests cost 0 credits. The live cost of every endpoint is listed on the pricing page and in the API reference, and each response reports its exact charge in the X-Credits-Used header."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there an enterprise plan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. If 80M credits/month on Max isn't enough, contact support@scrapebadger.com for a custom contract with dedicated proxy pools, higher rate tiers, and SLA."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get a refund?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"All purchases are final and non-refundable as a general rule. We may consider discretionary refunds for accidental purchases (within 7 days, no credits used), verified extended outages (>48h), or established customer goodwill. See our Refund & Cancellation Policy for details."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which payment methods do you accept?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Subscriptions are paid via Stripe (cards and other Stripe-supported methods). Pay As You Go top-ups can be paid via Stripe or crypto (via CoinGate)."}}]}</script><div class="min-h-screen bg-background overflow-x-clip"><div class="relative z-20 bg-secondary text-foreground border-b border-border"><div class="container mx-auto px-4"><a class="flex items-center justify-center gap-2 py-2 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity invisible" href="/announcements#0120f118-a2ee-4887-bcdd-4468f8a6e15d"><span><strong>Pricing update:</strong> <!-- -->new credit costs in effect since October 15</span><span class="hidden sm:inline px-2 py-0.5 bg-primary text-primary-foreground text-[10px] font-semibold rounded-md">Read more</span><span class="sm:hidden">→</span></a></div></div><header class="relative z-20 border-b border-border bg-background/80 backdrop-blur-sm"><div class="container mx-auto px-4"><nav class="flex items-center justify-between h-14 md:h-16"><a href="/"><div class="flex items